<title>HONG KONG: Swire to sell hotel for HK$2.2 bln - paper.</title>
<headline>Swire to sell hotel for HK$2.2 bln - paper.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swire Properties, a unit of Swire Pacific Ltd, has secured an agreement to sell 80 percent of its Marriott Hotel to a consortium for HK$2.2 billion, the Hong Kong Economic Journal said on Saturday.</p>
<p>The consortium included capital funding from the Singapore government, the newspaper quoted unidentified property sources as saying. It did not give the group's make-up.</p>
<p>The hotel's management contract would not be affected, the report said.</p>
<p>Swire officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
